<title>FRANCE: Elf strike continues, talks at 1400 GMT.</title>
<headline>Elf strike continues, talks at 1400 GMT.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Elf Aquitaine's three French oil refineries remained shut for a sixth day on Tuesday as strikers kept up a protest against cost savings and job cuts and Elf accused them of lengthening the strike with new demands.</p>
<p>An Elf spokesman said that what had started as a one-day protest strike last week was now aimed at securing early retirement and other benefits for shift workers whose jobs had never been threatened in the company's plans.</p>
<p>Unions said on Monday they had extended the strike until Tuesday evening after talks with bosses scheduled for 1400 GMT.</p>
<p>The Elf spokesman confirmed talks had been scheduled.</p>
</text>
